WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:07.259
Hey, this is really crazy video that people
are up in arms about because it is just so

00:00:07.259 --> 00:00:08.980
whacked out.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.730
This is video from July 30 first.

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:15.940
So the video is a month old, little over,
just over a month old, but it's somehow flew

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.160
under the radar until yesterday.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:23.550
Donald Trump did a roundtable on July 30,
first with the National Association of Police

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:31.330
Organizations leadership as a protest of is
as a sort of counterprogramming when protests

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:36.760
of police brutality were raging in the United
States at the time.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:44.210
And very similarly to Trump's recent statements
about what happened in Kenosha, about what's

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.929
going on in Portland.

00:00:45.929 --> 00:00:53.370
Trump at this event generalized that the protesters
are the violent anarchists and they are determined

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.499
to assault police officers.

00:00:55.499 --> 00:00:57.109
Police officers are in danger.

00:00:57.109 --> 00:01:01.289
Police officers are the victims, despite,
of course, being the ones who hold the power

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:04.460
in the power dynamic that exists with law
enforcement.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:13.060
And Trump went off on a tangent about protesters
throwing things frozen bottles of water, bricks,

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:14.060
whatever.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:22.310
And then Trump went into a one minute long,
bizarre attack on cans of soup and bags of

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:23.310
soup.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.550
What the hell is a bag of soup?

00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:30.179
The video somehow slipped under the radar
back on July 30 first.

00:01:30.179 --> 00:01:31.179
It is something else.

00:01:31.179 --> 00:01:32.609
Take a look at this.

00:01:32.609 --> 00:01:34.250
It's water.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:39.380
And then they have cans of soup, soup and
they throw the cans.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:42.649
So that's better than a brick because you
can't throw a brick.

00:01:42.649 --> 00:01:43.649
Too heavy.

00:01:43.649 --> 00:01:44.649
But a can of soup.

00:01:44.649 --> 00:01:45.649
You can really put some power into that, right?

00:01:45.649 --> 00:01:50.630
And then when they get caught, they say, oh,
this is soup for my family.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:51.630
They're so innocent.

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:52.829
This is soup for my family.

00:01:52.829 --> 00:01:54.080
It's incredible.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:59.380
And you have people coming over with bags
of soup, big bags of soup, and they lay it

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:03.810
on the ground and the anarchists take it and
they start throwing it at our cops and our

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:04.950
police.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:05.950
And it it hits you.

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:07.409
That's worse than a brick because it's got
force.

00:02:07.409 --> 00:02:09.580
It's the perfect size.

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.550
It's like made perfect.

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:17.190
And when they get caught, they say, no, this
is just soup for my family.

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.270
And then the media says, this is just soup.

00:02:19.270 --> 00:02:21.570
These people are very, very innocent.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:22.670
They're innocent people.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:25.640
These are just protesters.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:29.670
Is that wonderful to allow protesting now?

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:31.970
And by the way, the media knows it better
than we do.

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:32.970
They know what's going on.

00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:34.390
I don't know what's wrong with them.

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:35.890
They're doing our country.

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:41.680
So the extra component of bags of soup is
just extra funny.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.210
It reminds me of when Trump.

00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:50.780
In one of those montages for the RNC interviewed
workers who had recovered from covered.

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:53.730
And one worker said, I'm a custodian at the
post office.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.810
And Trump said, oh, what?

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:56.910
What do you do?

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.760
And it was just one of these moments where
Trump is just so out of touch, where he doesn't

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.990
understand what a custodian does.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:05.680
You know, most people who grew up in normal
childhoods know what a custodian does.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:10.700
That does or, you know, did, particularly
if if you're proficient in English.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:15.090
And this is a similar moment where Trump throws
in bags of soup.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:22.600
Now, I have seen pouches, Manish Shavitz,
you can get a sort of pouch of the dry ingredients,

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.240
which then you mix with water.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:28.310
But I don't know that Trump is talking about
those Manish Evatt's pouches when he talks

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:29.310
about bags of soup.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:33.170
But listen, I guess we have to take seriously
the weaponization of soup.

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:39.050
I've always actually been a little suspicious
of so-called alphabet soup.

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.360
That sounds weird to me.

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.210
I don't know that that that seems a little
bit dangerous to me.

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:49.140
Of course, you can only bag certain soups
like a bisque probably does not lend itself

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:50.930
to being bagged.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.620
But I've got a bag of chowder before.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:57.960
Both Manhattan and New England style clam
chowder really, really work well in a bag.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:04.170
This actually really is the exact type of
trump.

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:08.820
Going somewhere in his mind where we can't
tell whether it's a joke or something is wrong

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:09.820
with him.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:11.450
And of course, Trump has no sense of humor.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:13.540
So we very quickly end up at like.

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:15.990
Something seems to be very, very wrong with
this guy.

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:20.040
It's a delusional rant about weaponized soup.

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:22.770
And then, by the way, worse than bricks like
on the facts.

00:04:22.770 --> 00:04:25.120
I don't think that Trump is actually correct.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:27.500
And if you step back for just a moment.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.810
If this was your relative.

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:34.460
Wouldn't you immediately say they need a full
neuro psych eval?

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:38.810
Like when we interviewed Dr. Bandy Lee, I
guess it was three weeks ago now, two, three

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:47.230
weeks ago, and she said, you know, the symptoms
are there to warrant a neuro psych eval doesn't

00:04:47.230 --> 00:04:52.880
mean you're diagnosing anything, but there's
enough going on where you would want that.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:54.310
Does this qualify?

00:04:54.310 --> 00:05:00.180
Because this seems very, very strange and
it would be weird if it was anybody in your

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:01.180
family.

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:02.610
It happens to be the president of the United
States.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:06.410
And as usual, it's like, yeah, people wrote
to me about how funny this is.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:07.690
It is funny.

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:09.440
It's funny in a superficial way.

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:15.330
But once we're the laughing stock of the world
and we're the pity of the world, it's not

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:17.780
really all so funny anymore.

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:20.260
And it actually hasn't been funny for a long
time.

00:05:20.260 --> 00:05:23.760
Will we ever know the full truth of what is
behind rants like these?

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:28.630
Does anybody after the fact say, hey, Mr.
President, you know, sir, as he likes to say,

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:32.490
the material about weaponized bags of soup
that was not so good.

00:05:32.490 --> 00:05:34.680
That doesn't really resonate with with people.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:38.870
My belief at this point, given what we know
about Trump's personality, is that the people

00:05:38.870 --> 00:05:42.120
around him aren't willing to go up to him
and say that we know that anybody who's willing

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:44.730
to say to Trump what you're saying doesn't
make any sense.

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:45.810
They don't last very long.

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:50.230
And we've seen more than 500 people move on
from this administration over the last four

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:51.230
years.

00:05:51.230 --> 00:07:16.490
I just don't think it's welcome at all.

